SWEET WLAN level 7 firmware console (patch 0155, reads only). Once W16 has seen the shared-area address, the firmware runs 1 s longer, then the hnd_cons_t at shared word 5 (console_addr) is read as brcmfmac does (pcie.c:828-891: buffer address +8, size +12, write index +16) and the bytes 0..write index are printed as "SWEET WLAN: FW <line>" (CR dropped, lines cut at 120 characters, other non-printable bytes as '.'), then W17 as before.
Only under BAR2 window 0 after cfg 0x84 is back at 0: a console or buffer not entirely inside RAM below 0x400000, a size of 0 or above 64 KiB, or a write index beyond the size is logged and not read. No new store, no new tuple, no glue change.
Tests: shim/wlan_wr_host_test.c rune() console cases, tools/test_wlan_wr_mutants.py.

